WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.260
As air cools to saturation, water vapor can condense onto tiny

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.160
particles.

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.100
Droplets form and condensation releases heat.

00:00:09.595 --> 00:00:12.235
Evaporation is the reverse change.

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:16.070
Evaporation takes energy from the surroundings.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.970
Cloud droplets can collide and join into larger drops.

00:00:21.345 --> 00:00:25.585
A drop falls when its settling speed beats the updraft.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.920
Ice crystals can grow into snow.

00:00:28.345 --> 00:00:31.885
Supercooling means a drop has cooled below freezing and is

00:00:31.885 --> 00:00:33.025
still liquid.

00:00:33.405 --> 00:00:37.345
A strong updraft holds ice aloft while those drops freeze onto

00:00:37.345 --> 00:00:38.825
it and build hail.
